.TH TIMESHIFT-RECOVERY 8 "August 2026" "timeshift-recovery" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
timeshift-recovery \- provision a bootable Timeshift recovery environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B timeshift-recovery
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Timeshift snapshots kept on a remote host cannot be restored from a system
that will not boot: the restore tool, the network stack and the wireless
driver all live on the broken root filesystem.
.B timeshift-recovery
builds a small environment that carries its own copies, places it where GRUB
can reach it, and keeps it in step with the installed Timeshift. Pressing the
hotkey (default
.BR r )
while the machine starts boots the environment.
.PP
The environment is built with
.BR mmdebstrap (1)
against this host's own apt sources, so it always matches the installed
release and architecture. Timeshift itself is repacked from the installed
package with
.BR dpkg-repack (1),
and a dpkg trigger rebuilds the environment whenever Timeshift changes.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B build
Build the recovery environment into the local cache.
.TP
.B install
Build if needed, place the payload, and wire up GRUB.
.TP
.B upgrade
Rebuild and re-place an already installed environment.
.TP
.B enable
Restore the GRUB entry after \fBdisable\fR (instant; the payload never moved).
.TP
.B disable
Remove the GRUB entry but keep the payload, so \fBenable\fR is instant.
The disabled state survives package upgrades and the automatic refresh.
.TP
.B status
Show what is installed and whether it is current. With
.BR \-\-machine ,
print KEY=value lines for scripts.
.TP
.B reboot
Boot into the recovery environment once, now, without changing the default.
.TP
.B remove
Remove the payload, the GRUB entry, and the cached environment image
(which embeds credentials).
.TP
.B help, version
Show the usage message, or print the package version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-target " TARGET"
.BR auto " (default), " root ,
a partition such as \fI/dev/sdXN\fR, or a whole disk \fI/dev/sdX\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-size " SIZE"
Partition size when one is created (default 6G).
.TP
.BI \-\-hotkey " KEY"
Key to press at startup (default r).
.TP
.BI \-\-hotkey\-style " STYLE"
.BR hidden " (default), " countdown ", " menu ", or " none .
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " N"
Seconds GRUB waits for the hotkey (default 3).
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " N"
Display scale for the recovery GUI (default auto).
.TP
.BI \-\-hint " H"
Boot-screen hint while GRUB waits for the hotkey:
.BR splash " (default), " text ", or " none .
.TP
.BI \-\-timeshift\-deb " PATH"
Use this .deb instead of repacking the installed Timeshift.
.TP
.BI \-\-firmware " F"
.BR full " (default) or " slim .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ssh\-key, \-\-no\-wifi\-creds, \-\-no\-tailscale\-state
Do not embed the corresponding credential in the environment.
.TP
.B \-\-machine
With \fBstatus\fR: print KEY=value lines for scripts.
.TP
.B \-\-yes, \-y
Do not ask before writing a partition table.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run, \-n
Show what would happen, change nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Trace every command.
.SH SECURITY
Unless opted out, the environment embeds the SSH key from
.IR /etc/timeshift/ssh ,
saved Wi-Fi passphrases, and the Tailscale node identity, so an unattended
restore works on a machine that is already broken. They are readable by
anyone who can boot this machine or read the recovery media. Restrict the
key on the backup host, for example in its authorized_keys:
.PP
.nf
    restrict,command="rrsync -ro /path/to/snapshots" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/timeshift-recovery/config
Defaults for every option above.
.TP
.I /var/cache/timeshift-recovery/
The built environment image (root-only; embeds credentials).
.TP
.I /var/lib/timeshift-recovery/
Installed-state records and, for the root-filesystem target, the payload.
.TP
.I /var/log/timeshift-recovery.log
Session log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR timeshift (1),
.BR mmdebstrap (1),
.BR dpkg-repack (1)
